# File spec for ./validate.rs. The sibling lint spec is cross-referenced for the check
# division; the Rhai script lane is a packaged asset owned by /agent/agent.sdd.

Spec: PackageValidate

Platform: Rust

Purpose:
  The `agent package validate` leaf: run the shipped Rhai `validate` module against the
    source tree's package.yaml. The Rust side only assembles the Rhai engine, injects
    @Parameters as the script variable `args`, evaluates `import("validate")` plus
    `validate::run(args)`, and hands any script failure back as @common::Result::Err for
    the caller's exit-4 trap; the manifest-schema checking itself lives in the script lane.

Owns:
  ./validate.rs

References:
  ./mod.sdd — caller and exit lane: every @Err from @run prints
    `The package failed to validate: {e:}` via @tracing::error! then
    @std::process::exit(4); this file logs nothing and never exits.
  ./lint.sdd — pending sibling spec, cross-reference only: lint owns the tree/structure
    and template-script findings, this leaf the manifest schema gate (see `Must not`).
  /agent/scripts/packages/validate.rhai — the module today's `validate` import resolves to
    (asset owned by /agent/agent.sdd scripts tree, its own spec pending); the checks
    frozen below read through it.

Must:
  Build the engine as @common::rhaihandler::Script::new over resolver dirs appended in
    exactly this order: `<source>/scripts`, `<script-dir>/packages`, `<script-dir>/lib` —
    strings via @PathBuf::to_string_lossy @Display formatting, never existence-checked; first
    resolver dir holding a `validate` module wins, so a package-authored
    `<source>/scripts/validate.rhai` shadows the shipped module for its own validation.
  Inject @Parameters as the script global `args` through the Deref'd
    @vynil_core::engine::Script::set_dynamic: a JSON map of the two private fields under key
    names `source` and `script_dir` (path text), visible to this @Script's later evaluations;
    the shipped module reads only `args.source` and builds the manifest path by `+`-joined
    concatenation, so a trailing separator in the flag value yields a doubled slash.
  Evaluate exactly one snippet — `import("validate") as validate;` then
    `validate::run(args);` — discard the resulting @rhai::Dynamic via @let, and return
    @Ok(@common::Result type unit); the verdict channel is script error versus completion,
    never an inspected return value.
  Leave every user-visible text to the caller trap: no @println, no @tracing call, and no
    filesystem or cluster write from this lane; the checks performed are strictly the
    imported module's — for the shipped script that is `<source>/package.yaml` readable at
    all, then key presence `apiVersion`/`kind`/`metadata`, `metadata` string members
    `name`/`category`/`type`, `options`-is-map, `requirements`-is-array-or-absent, then a
    strict @read_package_yaml model re-read, then the @validate_options shape gate.

Must not:
  Run structure, directory-layout, file-presence, Handlebars or Rhai-quality checks —
    lint scans that (`./lint.sdd`); validate reads no file and walks no tree itself.
  Initialize a cluster context (@common::context::init_k8s) or reach the engine's k8s, http, s3
    or OCI registrations as part of this contract — @Script::new installs them, but the
    validate flow is offline, matching ./mod.sdd's no-init-at-dispatch posture.

Depends on:
  @common::rhaihandler::Script (/common/src/rhaihandler.sdd) — @Script::new
    resolver/engine assembly and @Script::eval's error conversion; the Deref'd core
    `set_dynamic` injection leg carries core's own unwraps.
  @common::Result and @common::Error::SerializationError (/common/src/lib.sdd) — the return
    lane and the sole explicit error mapping.
  /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd — script names `read_package_yaml`, `validate_options` and
    the @VynilPackageSource / @Schema acceptance they enforce.
  /common/src/yamlhandler.sdd and `vynil-core` `0.7.7` — `yaml_decode` and `file_read` come
    from the core generic set installed by @Script::new (attributed per rhaihandler.sdd),
    not from this file.
  @clap::Args, @serde::Serialize, @serde_json, @std::path::PathBuf — flag glue and the
    args-map injection.
  ./mod.sdd — the only caller of @run.

Exposes:
  @Parameters — `#[derive(@clap::Args, @Debug, @serde::Serialize, @serde::Deserialize)]`
    struct with both fields private, so the `args` JSON map is the only channel by which the
    script sees them; `@Debug` serves the @Debug derive on @Commands in ./mod.sdd.
    Field `source` — doc help `Source directory`, short `-o`, long `--source`,
    env `SOURCE`, value name `SOURCE`, default `/src`; the `-o` short is why source is not
    `-s` (see Tasks).
    Field `script_dir` — doc help `Agent script directory`, short `-s`, long
    `--script-dir`, env `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, value name `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY`, default
    `./agent/scripts` — the same env name and default the lint leaf uses for the same dir.
  @run — `pub fn @run(@args: &@Parameters) -> @common::Result<@()>`; sync like every
    package leaf (./mod.sdd).

Accepts:
  A clap-parsed @Parameters by reference; paths are taken as given, relative or absolute,
    with no existence, type or UTF-8 validation — a missing manifest or unresolvable
    `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY` fails later as a script error, never as an input error here.
  Non-UTF-8 path components degrade via @PathBuf lossy rendering into both the resolver
    strings and the `args.source` text the script concatenates.

Returns:
  @Ok with the module's unit value discarded — silent success, no stdout or stderr from
    this file; whether the process then exits 0 is ./../main.rs's lane (spec pending).

Raises:
  @common::Error::SerializationError — explicit @map_err on the @serde_json::to_value of
    @Parameters; the value is two pathname strings, so no input reaching here through clap
    drives that leg in practice (see Tasks).
  @common::Error::Core wrapping the core Rhai error from @Script::eval, display prefixed
    `Rhai script error: ` (conversion frozen by rhaihandler.sdd), covering: the `validate`
    import unresolvable in all three resolver dirs or failing to parse; script throws from
    the shipped module (`You should set your apiVersion`, `You should set your kind`,
    `No metadata defined in package.yaml`, `No metadata.{key} defined in package.yaml`,
    `metadata.{key} should be a string`, `options should be a map.`,
    `requirements should be an array.`); `file_read` stdio failure when
    `<source>/package.yaml` is missing or unreadable; `yaml_decode` parse failure; the
    strict serde-model rejection (`read_package_yaml` adding required
    `metadata.description`, `metadata.features`, the `type` enum values and requirement
    shapes); and the `validate_options` rejection (`Json decoding error: …`, gate owned by
    /common/src/vynilpackage.sdd).
  A @set_dynamic panic channel exists through the Deref'd core method's internal unwraps
    (rhaihandler.sdd), unreachable from this file because only an already-built JSON value
    is injected.

Handles:
  The discarded @rhai::Dynamic last value of `validate::run(args)` — completion alone marks
    success, whatever the module returns (`yaml` map in the shipped script's case).
  Absent `requirements` key — the module silently assigns `[]` to its decoded copy, which
    @run discards; the strict re-read still demands the key (Tasks records the effect).
  A package-local `validate` module — resolves first by resolver order and replaces the
    shipped checks entirely, no diagnostics about the shadowing.
  All failure branches converge: no logging, no partial output, nothing to clean up —
    this file mutates no state.

Tasks:
  [ ] Cover @run with tests for the scenarios below: no #[cfg(test)] module exists in this
      file and no integration test drives `package validate` (the `validate` text in
      agent/tests is unrelated fixture data).
  [?] The `source` flag answers to short `-o` while every sibling uses `-s` only for
      script dir; decide whether `-o` is frozen or a `-S`-style short is added.
  [?] @Parameters derives @serde::Deserialize that nothing consumes — fields are private
      and the only serde use is @Serialize; decide whether the derive stays or goes.
  [?] "Validate a package" is schema-shaped only: any non-empty `apiVersion`/`kind` string
      passes (values are never compared to `vynil.solidite.fr/v1` / `Package`), empty
      metadata strings pass, and no file-presence or directory rule is checked — the gate
      is weaker than the name promises. Decide with ./lint.sdd which checks each command
      owns.
  [?] The resolver order makes `<source>/scripts/validate.rhai` a total override of the
      shipped validation — decide whether that is an intended authoring extension or needs
      to be locked to the packaged scripts.
  [?] The script's defaulting of a missing `requirements` key into the decoded map is dead
      — @run re-reads the file through the serde model, which lists `requirements` as
      required — so the lenient lane silently rescues nothing; decide whether the model
      gains a serde default or the script drop is removed.
  [?] @common::Error::SerializationError is mapped but unreachable for clap-built args of
      two path fields; decide whether the map_err stays as defensive code.

Done when:
  The scenarios below carry mapped tests for both the silent-@Ok and the error-to-exit-4
    lanes, the script-boundary decisions above are recorded, and `cargo test -p agent` with
    clippy and fmt stay green.

Scenario: compliant package validates silently
  Given a source tree whose package.yaml satisfies every shipped-script throw plus the
    strict @VynilPackageSource model and the options shape gate
  When @run executes
  Then @Ok is returned with no output written by this file, and ./mod.sdd's trap never fires
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: metadata throw surfaces verbatim through the exit-4 trap
  Given a package.yaml with no `apiVersion` key
  When @run executes
  Then @run returns @Err displaying `Rhai script error: ` over `You should set your apiVersion`
  And ./mod.sdd logs `The package failed to validate: {e:}` and exits with code 4
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: missing manifest is a script read failure not an input check
  Given a source directory holding no package.yaml
  When @run executes under the default `--source /src` or any other path
  Then the @Err is the `file_read` stdio failure converted by @Script::eval — this leaf adds
    no dedicated missing-manifest case, so the message is generic rather than
    `Missing package manifest` as lint renders it
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: package shadow module replaces the whole check
  Given `<source>/scripts/validate.rhai` with a `run(args)` body that throws nothing, over a
    package.yaml the shipped module would reject
  When @run executes
  Then the package's own module resolves first and @Ok is returned — shipped checks bypassed,
    shadowing unlogged
  No mapped test exists.

Scenario: misconfigured script dir fails even a valid package
  Given `SCRIPT_DIRECTORY` pointing at a tree with no packages/validate.rhai and no
    package-local shadow, and an otherwise fully valid package.yaml
  When @run executes
  Then the import fails and @Err surfaces an import/module error — an environment mistake is
    indistinguishable from a bad package at the CLI
  No mapped test exists.

Example:
  defaults inject `args` = `{"source":"/src","script_dir":"./agent/scripts"}` and resolver
    dirs `/src/scripts`, `./agent/scripts/packages`, `./agent/scripts/lib`
  a flag pair as `agent package validate -o ./pkg -s ../scripts` feeds resolver dirs
    `./pkg/scripts`, `../scripts/packages`, `../scripts/lib` and manifest path
    `./pkg/package.yaml`
